1
00:02:05,325 --> 00:02:07,498
You look like you're doing all right.

2
00:02:09,896 --> 00:02:12,672
Father Time has his way with us all.

3
00:02:13,900 --> 00:02:15,902
Looks like you must have pissed him off.

4
00:02:24,244 --> 00:02:25,245
Ahem.

5
00:02:25,746 --> 00:02:27,123
Why we here?

6
00:02:29,016 --> 00:02:32,828
All right. You know that thing
the State PD is asking about,

7
00:02:32,919 --> 00:02:35,092
the Lake Charles murder.

8
00:02:36,156 --> 00:02:39,865
Shouldn't that have been in the papers
or online somewhere by now'?

9
00:02:41,128 --> 00:02:43,506
I mean, we can't trust them.

10
00:02:43,597 --> 00:02:45,770
I mean, if they go cover
something like that up,

11
00:02:45,832 --> 00:02:47,778
who knows what else they've covered up.

12
00:02:48,502 --> 00:02:49,947
What you think?

13
00:02:51,672 --> 00:02:56,121
I think you don't look particularly
healthy, listening to you talk.

14
00:02:56,510 --> 00:03:00,788
Your eyes, you seem kind of brittle, Rust.

15
00:03:01,615 --> 00:03:05,188
Most of the last decade
I spent stone drunk.

16
00:03:05,652 --> 00:03:08,064
Functional, but hammered.

17
00:03:08,989 --> 00:03:13,495
Went back to Alaska. Spent eight
years working fishing boats, bars.

18
00:03:13,660 --> 00:03:15,571
Oh, I thought you didn't like the cold.

19
00:03:15,662 --> 00:03:17,073
I hate it.

20
00:03:17,164 --> 00:03:20,407
And then I come back hereto Louisiana
for the first time in 2010.

21
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:22,138
And why is that?

22
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:25,815
The same reason I'm sitting
across the table from you now.

23
00:03:27,074 --> 00:03:29,213
A man remembers his debts.

24
00:03:31,645 --> 00:03:33,488
I don't dwell in the past.

25
00:03:34,347 --> 00:03:35,883
Well, it must be nice.

26
00:03:35,982 --> 00:03:39,191
I'm not interested in whatever
it is you think you owe me.

27
00:03:39,252 --> 00:03:40,856
Well, I don't owe you.

28
00:03:40,921 --> 00:03:44,027
We left something undone.

29
00:03:44,658 --> 00:03:46,535
We got to fix it.

30
00:03:46,593 --> 00:03:49,870
I've been working on this for two years.
Me. Myself.

31
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:51,910
I never called you.
I never bothered you with it.

32
00:03:51,998 --> 00:03:53,238
Yeah, why would you?

33
00:03:53,333 --> 00:03:56,906
Shit, man! What, did you alienate
every other person in your life

34
00:03:57,003 --> 00:03:59,244
and then finally you came back
to me in the rotation?

35
00:03:59,339 --> 00:04:00,283
You know, not for nothing,

36
00:04:00,373 --> 00:04:02,375
but if you hadn't clipped Ledoux back then,

37
00:04:02,442 --> 00:04:04,888
we might have got the whole fucking story
out of him.

38
00:04:06,513 --> 00:04:10,051
You know, I think I'm going to
finish this beer and say so long.

39
00:04:10,117 --> 00:04:12,119
I'm not much of a drinker nowadays.

40
00:04:12,219 --> 00:04:15,200
In fact, I hadn't had a drop in three weeks
till I ran into you.

41
00:04:15,255 --> 00:04:17,257
I don't need you to drink, Marty.

42
00:04:17,357 --> 00:04:19,394
- I need you to help me.
- Why would I?

43
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,897
They say you can't account for your time.

44
00:04:21,962 --> 00:04:26,104
They got eyewitnesses placing you
at the Lake Charles crime scene.

45
00:04:26,199 --> 00:04:28,975
You got some storage shed
that you won't let 'em look at.

46
00:04:29,069 --> 00:04:30,446
- That's right.
- Why not?

47
00:04:30,537 --> 00:04:33,040
Why not shoot straight with them?
You're innocent.

48
00:04:33,106 --> 00:04:34,779
Help them stop wasting their time.

49
00:04:34,875 --> 00:04:38,152
Fucking since when did guilt
and innocence define the State PD, huh'?

50
00:04:38,712 --> 00:04:40,316
Come the fuck on!

51
00:04:40,413 --> 00:04:42,333
I don't know the sprawl of this thing,
all right?

52
00:04:42,382 --> 00:04:46,558
The people I'm after, they're all fucking
over. They're in a lot of different things.

53
00:04:46,620 --> 00:04:48,622
Pieces. Family trees.

54
00:04:49,556 --> 00:04:53,129
The only way for you to understand
what I'm onto here is for me to show you.

55
00:04:53,226 --> 00:04:55,297
You got to come see what I got.

56
00:04:55,896 --> 00:04:57,466
No. You know what?

57
00:04:57,564 --> 00:05:00,272
I don't think I've been
very clear with you, Rust.

58
00:05:00,333 --> 00:05:04,076
If you were drowning,
I'd throw you a fucking barbell.

59
00:05:04,805 --> 00:05:07,809
Why would I ever help you?

60
00:05:14,014 --> 00:05:16,494
Because you have a debt.

61
00:05:26,259 --> 00:05:28,261
You got some fucking sack.

62
00:05:28,528 --> 00:05:31,168
What's that mean, I have a debt, huh?

63
00:05:31,264 --> 00:05:34,609
Means the way shit went down in '95,

64
00:05:34,668 --> 00:05:36,773
this is on you, too, buddy.

65
00:05:45,345 --> 00:05:47,484
What do you got to show me?

66
00:07:03,023 --> 00:07:04,559
What you packing?

67
00:07:08,228 --> 00:07:09,866
.38.

68
00:07:11,398 --> 00:07:12,741
Hollow-point?

69
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:14,578
Yeah.

70
00:07:14,634 --> 00:07:16,204
That'll do it.

71
00:07:25,312 --> 00:07:27,724
You can never be too careful.

72
00:07:44,297 --> 00:07:48,074
All right, remember
there was no physical evidence

73
00:07:48,234 --> 00:07:52,148
connecting Dora Lange to
Ledoux's place out in the woods.

74
00:07:52,238 --> 00:07:56,653
Meaning it probably didn't happen out there.
Nobody was in a hurry to bring that up.

75
00:07:56,743 --> 00:08:00,418
Two. Women and children going missing.

76
00:08:00,480 --> 00:08:04,121
All taken from areas within
a 10-mile radius of schools

77
00:08:04,184 --> 00:08:06,994
that were funded by
Tuttle's Wellspring initiative.

78
00:08:07,087 --> 00:08:10,591
We establish a connection,
who's in, who's out, you know?

79
00:08:10,657 --> 00:08:14,264
I mean, do people disappear in equal
numbers in other parts of the state?

80
00:08:14,361 --> 00:08:17,171
- How many schools were there?
- Fourteen.

81
00:08:17,263 --> 00:08:19,504
Now, I've covered a surface area.

82
00:08:19,599 --> 00:08:22,705
I pulled runaways in state
and missing persons.

83
00:08:22,802 --> 00:08:26,443
Now, if you'll notice, there's twice as
many along the bayous. I don't know why.

84
00:08:26,506 --> 00:08:28,782
Hell, someone should do a study as to why.

85
00:08:29,442 --> 00:08:31,285
Now you're just throwing up stats.

86
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:34,348
Why was Turtle so interested
in the Lange case, huh?

87
00:08:34,514 --> 00:08:37,688
Remember Charlie Lange
said what Ledoux told him?

88
00:08:37,784 --> 00:08:40,196
He said there's a group of men, sacrifices.

89
00:08:40,286 --> 00:08:42,789
Well, I think Turtle recognized the scene.

90
00:08:42,856 --> 00:08:45,860
That's why he came down there
jiminy quick with a fucking taskforce,

91
00:08:45,959 --> 00:08:48,337
and that's why he tripped out
when I talked to him in '02.

92
00:08:48,395 --> 00:08:50,204
Okay, so what happened to him?

93
00:08:50,997 --> 00:08:55,878
I mean, I'm looking around here
and I don't see or hear anything

94
00:08:55,969 --> 00:08:57,880
that doesn't make this all conjectural.

95
00:08:59,139 --> 00:09:01,085
1988.

96
00:09:01,207 --> 00:09:06,486
Accusations of child molestation
at a preschool funded by Tuttle.

97
00:09:06,546 --> 00:09:09,152
The name of that school
was Shepherd's Flock.

98
00:09:09,249 --> 00:09:12,719
It shuts down, reopens two years
later on Pelican Island

99
00:09:12,819 --> 00:09:17,325
under the name Light of the Way Academy,
where Rianne Olivier went.

100
00:09:17,390 --> 00:09:20,564
Now, I got an enrollment list.
Sixteen kids in the class.

101
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,367
One of them turned out to be a young man

102
00:09:22,429 --> 00:09:25,239
who just showed up
for solicitation in New Orleans.

103
00:09:31,004 --> 00:09:35,578
Now this is 2010.
His name is Toby Boelert.

104
00:09:35,942 --> 00:09:38,081
Goes by the name of Johnny Joanie.

105
00:09:47,353 --> 00:09:49,196
Shepherd's Flock.

106
00:09:50,523 --> 00:09:53,265
Why are you asking me about that place?

107
00:09:53,359 --> 00:09:57,466
After that place shut down,
there was a lot of talk going around...

108
00:09:58,765 --> 00:10:00,540
You ever see that reverend,

109
00:10:01,468 --> 00:10:03,038
Billy Lee Tuttle, around?

110
00:10:03,103 --> 00:10:06,482
You know, I think so.
But who can remember way back?

111
00:10:07,107 --> 00:10:08,814
That's how it all started.

112
00:10:09,309 --> 00:10:11,550
Memory be fucked.

113
00:10:12,645 --> 00:10:16,650
I decided it all had to be a dream anyways.
And I don't remember if...

114
00:10:20,053 --> 00:10:21,430
We'd go to sleep.

115
00:10:22,889 --> 00:10:26,132
Only sometimes I didn't feel like I was
asleep. I felt like I was still awake.

116
00:10:26,226 --> 00:10:29,139
But I must have been asleep
because I couldn't move.

117
00:10:29,662 --> 00:10:33,576
Just sort of see under my eyelids.

118
00:10:34,501 --> 00:10:35,980
Then what?

119
00:10:36,769 --> 00:10:38,476
I don't know.

120
00:10:38,571 --> 00:10:40,073
There were men,

121
00:10:41,574 --> 00:10:43,611
taking pictures.

122
00:10:44,410 --> 00:10:48,017
Sometimes other things.

123
00:10:48,615 --> 00:10:51,755
- Who were they?
- I don't know.

124
00:10:51,818 --> 00:10:54,094
They had animal faces.

125
00:10:54,154 --> 00:10:56,930
That's why I decided it had to be a dream.

126
00:10:56,990 --> 00:11:00,267
They had animal faces.
Well, it had to be a dream.

127
00:11:00,326 --> 00:11:02,636
Any other kids see this?

128
00:11:02,695 --> 00:11:03,696
One girl.

129
00:11:05,031 --> 00:11:09,173
I don't remember her name.
She first started talking about it.

130
00:11:09,269 --> 00:11:11,647
She seen it, too, the faces.

131
00:11:11,704 --> 00:11:15,015
- I do not remember her name.
- Marie Fontenot.

132
00:11:17,110 --> 00:11:18,316
Maybe.

133
00:11:19,279 --> 00:11:21,384
You ever see any of these men's faces?

134
00:11:21,481 --> 00:11:24,724
Once. They didn't all have animal faces.

135
00:11:26,953 --> 00:11:31,163
Three younger men. I don't remember them.
Just one.

136
00:11:31,824 --> 00:11:34,202
He had bad scars all around his mouth.

137
00:11:34,294 --> 00:11:37,207
Like the bottom half got all burned up.

138
00:11:39,165 --> 00:11:41,042
And you know what?

139
00:11:41,134 --> 00:11:44,013
I thought that meant it was a dream, too.

140
00:11:47,006 --> 00:11:49,885
No, I don't think it was a dream.

141
00:11:51,044 --> 00:11:52,084
HART". I don't understand.

142
00:11:52,178 --> 00:11:56,388
Are you saying that you think
that this hypothetical killer

143
00:11:56,482 --> 00:11:59,156
was, uh, an old school teacher?

144
00:11:59,219 --> 00:12:02,689
Or it might, what, involve State PD?

145
00:12:02,755 --> 00:12:05,395
Goddamn, what happened to you, man?

146
00:12:06,426 --> 00:12:08,872
You remember him? Hmm?

147
00:12:09,696 --> 00:12:11,437
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

148
00:12:11,531 --> 00:12:13,738
You and I are on the case in Erath.

149
00:12:13,833 --> 00:12:16,439
A girl comes forward and says
she was chased through the woods

150
00:12:16,536 --> 00:12:18,675
by a spaghetti monster with green ears.

151
00:12:18,738 --> 00:12:23,710
Now I think that this is our man
with the scars on his face.

152
00:12:23,776 --> 00:12:25,449
I've got three references.

153
00:12:25,545 --> 00:12:30,051
Seventeen years ago, that old revival church
said a tall man with scars came through.

154
00:12:30,116 --> 00:12:35,122
Kelly Reider, in the hospital. And, now,
this hooker from the Quarter, Toby.

155
00:12:35,221 --> 00:12:36,928
I don't know who he is.
I don't know where he is.

156
00:12:37,023 --> 00:12:40,732
I don't know where this thing fucking
starts, but it ends with him.

157
00:12:42,262 --> 00:12:44,868
All right, you know that little township
down around Erath?

158
00:12:44,931 --> 00:12:48,105
All right?
That's where the Turtle family is from.

159
00:12:48,201 --> 00:12:50,875
Now, it used to be a pirate hideout.

160
00:12:50,970 --> 00:12:53,473
Now they turned it
into plantations or whatnot.

161
00:12:53,573 --> 00:12:56,144
Had a very rural sense of Mardi Gras.

162
00:12:57,310 --> 00:13:00,052
Uh, you know, the men on horses,
animal masks, and such.

163
00:13:00,113 --> 00:13:02,821
- Courir de Mardi Gras.
- That's right.

164
00:13:02,915 --> 00:13:07,125
Now, they had an annual winter festival,
all right, heavy on the Saturnalia.

165
00:13:07,220 --> 00:13:10,793
A place where that Santeria
and Voudon all mashed together.

166
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:11,891
Have a look.

167
00:13:11,958 --> 00:13:13,904
From the winter festival.

168
00:13:15,261 --> 00:13:16,569
Blindfold.

169
00:13:17,430 --> 00:13:19,432
Antlers. Mask.

170
00:13:21,467 --> 00:13:26,610
I got these from a series an artist
did in Kenner, right after Katrina.

171
00:13:26,673 --> 00:13:31,281
Says he kept running across these
"stick things" as he called them.

172
00:13:31,344 --> 00:13:32,846
Look familiar?

173
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:37,118
I think our man had a real good time
after the hurricane.

174
00:13:37,617 --> 00:13:40,860
Chaos. People missing. People gone.

175
00:13:40,953 --> 00:13:42,296
Cops gone.

176
00:13:43,289 --> 00:13:45,428
I think he had a real good year.

177
00:13:45,992 --> 00:13:47,938
What do you need me for'?

178
00:13:48,961 --> 00:13:53,933
You got friends on the force.
You have access that I don't. Databases.

179
00:13:54,100 --> 00:13:57,604
I need case files. I need missing persons.
I need homicides.

180
00:13:57,670 --> 00:14:00,344
I need title transfers, auto and home.

181
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:03,182
I got a list of names. I'm gonna need
background checks, tax records.

182
00:14:03,276 --> 00:14:04,983
Anything we can get on Ledoux.

183
00:14:05,044 --> 00:14:06,387
Jesus Christ, man.

184
00:14:06,479 --> 00:14:09,358
I wouldn't have called you
and I wouldn't have fucking bothered you

185
00:14:09,449 --> 00:14:12,055
if State wouldn't have pulled me in
on this Lake Charles case.

186
00:14:12,151 --> 00:14:13,653
Well, if you need help,

187
00:14:13,720 --> 00:14:16,462
why don't you just give it
to Papania and Gilbough?

188
00:14:16,522 --> 00:14:19,082
No, they may be pawns in this thing
and not even fucking know it.

189
00:14:19,158 --> 00:14:20,660
- Come on.
- Look, Eddie Tuttle

190
00:14:20,727 --> 00:14:22,866
is the goddamn senator of this state.

191
00:14:22,962 --> 00:14:25,738
The late Reverend Billy Lee Turtle
is his cousin.

192
00:14:25,832 --> 00:14:27,812
I'm telling you, it's a
fucking family thing.

193
00:14:27,867 --> 00:14:30,370
That's what I mean
when I talk about the sprawl, Marty.

194
00:14:30,470 --> 00:14:33,576
Eddie Tuttle is the reason that
the Lake Charles thing never made the wire.

195
00:14:33,673 --> 00:14:36,381
Look, man' you have
some compelling stuff here.

196
00:14:36,476 --> 00:14:38,319
And you might have something.

197
00:14:41,247 --> 00:14:46,856
But all this "sprawl," as you call it,
which I would call "conjecture,"

198
00:14:46,986 --> 00:14:49,592
this shit about the
Tuttles and the State PD,

199
00:14:49,689 --> 00:14:53,569
do you know how fucking crazy that sounds?

200
00:14:53,659 --> 00:14:55,935
It's like you've been alone too long.

201
00:14:56,028 --> 00:15:02,240
Like you, maybe, told yourself this story
and kept drinking until you believed it.

202
00:15:02,335 --> 00:15:03,575
Marty.

203
00:15:07,173 --> 00:15:10,848
I had my time where I wondered
if this was all in my head.

204
00:15:12,545 --> 00:15:14,218
That time passed.

205
00:15:15,181 --> 00:15:16,524
Really?

206
00:15:21,521 --> 00:15:24,400
What happened to Billy Lee Tuttle?

207
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:30,707
There's something
you're going to have to look at.

208
00:15:31,864 --> 00:15:33,207
No other way around it.

209
00:15:38,304 --> 00:15:39,944
You still take your coffee black?

210
00:15:40,706 --> 00:15:42,947
Oh, uh, green tea,
if you have it.

211
00:15:43,042 --> 00:15:45,784
I've been trying to stay away
from coffee, you know,

212
00:15:45,878 --> 00:15:47,653
a little bit healthier.

213
00:15:47,747 --> 00:15:51,388
So, Mace, is she, uh,
back from Chicago yet?

214
00:15:51,584 --> 00:15:54,724
- Mmm-hmm, three months ago.
- Three months?

215
00:15:55,087 --> 00:15:56,088
Uh...

216
00:15:57,256 --> 00:15:59,793
- What was that? That...
- AmeriCorps.

217
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:02,597
- Oh.
Leaching.

218
00:16:02,662 --> 00:16:04,573
And Audrey, how is she?

219
00:16:04,630 --> 00:16:07,133
She's fine at the moment.

220
00:16:07,233 --> 00:16:10,578
She sometimes decides
she doesn't need her meds.

221
00:16:11,404 --> 00:16:14,578
I like her boyfriend.
He watches out for her.

222
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:17,484
She had an art show in New Orleans.

223
00:16:17,577 --> 00:16:18,954
Sold some paintings.

224
00:16:19,011 --> 00:16:24,791
Well, that's good. That's great. I should
buy one, I mean, if I can afford it.

225
00:16:29,856 --> 00:16:32,302
So the reason I, uh...

226
00:16:32,358 --> 00:16:35,305
I mean, like I said on the phone,

227
00:16:35,361 --> 00:16:37,602
I want to ask you about those cops.

228
00:16:38,931 --> 00:16:41,468
They just wanted to know
about you and Rust.

229
00:16:41,601 --> 00:16:42,944
Mostly Rust.

230
00:16:43,002 --> 00:16:47,144
They wanted to know about the fight in '02.

231
00:16:51,010 --> 00:16:53,684
- Mmm' did you tell them?
- No.

232
00:16:54,947 --> 00:16:57,120
But they think Rust did something.

233
00:16:58,284 --> 00:17:00,662
I know. He didn't.

234
00:17:00,786 --> 00:17:02,697
I didn't think he did.

235
00:17:08,027 --> 00:17:10,633
You talk to him?

236
00:17:13,399 --> 00:17:15,345
No. Not since.

237
00:17:16,636 --> 00:17:17,637
You?

238
00:17:18,404 --> 00:17:22,011
Yeah. I mean, after they brought me in.
Yeah.

239
00:17:23,409 --> 00:17:26,253
- How is he?
Different. Same.

240
00:17:26,345 --> 00:17:29,849
I mean, he's lived rough
for a long time now.

241
00:17:32,018 --> 00:17:34,225
He always did, it seemed like.

242
00:17:34,987 --> 00:17:36,523
Taken a toll.

243
00:17:39,258 --> 00:17:41,101
He needs my help.

244
00:17:42,094 --> 00:17:43,767
Are you going to help him?

245
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:48,739
